	(text "Power notes (plans/usb-power.md):\n- Load sharing: VBUS -> D7 -> VSYS with USB, VBAT -> Q1 -> VSYS on battery (Q1 gate on VBUS). The charger only sees the battery, so it terminates.\n- Q2: battery reverse-polarity guard (drain on J3, gate to GND via R6). The gauge reads ~5-30 mV off under load.\n- JP3 picks the charge current: 1-2 = R21 2k (500 mA, default), 2-3 = R33 10k (100 mA). JP1 / JP2: cut to measure the VBAT / 3V3 drain.\n- U13 TPS7A2033 (3.3 V) + U14 TPS7A2018 (1.8 V) = VS1053 only (+3.3VA analog + IO, +1V8 core). Both EN on VS_EN (PA6), R8 100k pull-down: off until the MCU enables them. JP6: cut to measure the VS1053 drain.\n- JP4 picks VS1053 AVDD/IOVDD: U13 out (default, switched by VS_EN) or the 3V3 through FB3 (always on). +3.3VA follows VBAT below ~3.4 V: firmware cutoff >= 3.2 V.\n- NT1: single GND-GNDA tie, place it under the VS1053 AGND pins.\n- PCB: bat-man1 EP (pin 9) needs GND copper + vias (~1 W at charge start). D8 (VBUS TVS) next to USB1. L3 = Murata DFE252012P-R47M (2.5x2.0 mm, end terminals: hand-solderable, Isat 5.7 A).\n- U11 (TPS63802), U12 (MAX17048 TDFN), U13/U14 (TPS7A20 SOT-23, JLC only has clones) are not stocked at JLC: source them separately."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 16.51 193.548 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "9a878b4e-4a3c-47c4-9765-779c9476c963")
	)
